UnitLiquidity::AddLiquidity
├── when the recipient is the zero address
│   └── it should revert with InvalidRecipient
└── given the recipient is not the zero address
    ├── when the factory is not approved
    │   └── it should revert with FactoryNotApproved
    └── given the factory is approved
        ├── when the resolved pool holds a different pair
        │   └── it should revert with PoolTokenMismatch
        ├── when the factory has no pool and creation is not requested
        │   └── it should revert with PoolNotFound
        ├── when the factory has no pool and creation is requested
        │   ├── it should create the pool through the factory
        │   ├── it should push both funded amounts to the created pool
        │   └── it should mint to _recipient
        ├── when a stable and a volatile factory each resolve their own pool
        │   ├── it should deposit into the pool of the selected factory
        │   └── it should mint to _recipient
        ├── when the pair is passed in reverse pool order
        │   ├── it should trim the deposit with the realigned reserves
        │   ├── it should push the trimmed amounts to the pool
        │   └── it should mint to _recipient
        ├── when token A has an external payer and charges a fee on transfer
        │   ├── it should pull the requested token A amount from _caller
        │   ├── it should push the measured received token A amount to the pool
        │   └── it should mint to _recipient
        ├── given the pool is unseeded
        │   ├── when the funded token A is below its minimum
        │   │   └── it should revert with InsufficientAmountA
        │   ├── when the funded token B is below its minimum
        │   │   └── it should revert with InsufficientAmountB
        │   └── given both funded amounts meet their minimums
        │       ├── when the recipient is the router
        │       │   ├── it should push both funded amounts to the pool
        │       │   ├── it should track the minted lp token
        │       │   └── it should mint to _recipient
        │       └── when the recipient is not the router
        │           ├── it should push both funded amounts to the pool
        │           └── it should mint to _recipient
        └── given the pool is seeded
            ├── when the minted liquidity is below its minimum
            │   └── it should revert with InsufficientLiquidityMinted
            ├── when the minted liquidity equals its minimum
            │   └── it should accept the minted liquidity
            ├── given the full token B quote fits uint
            │   ├── given the optimal token B does not exceed the funded token B
            │   │   ├── when the floored token B quote equals the funded amount
            │   │   │   ├── it should push both funded amounts to the pool
            │   │   │   └── it should mint to _recipient
            │   │   ├── when the optimal token B is below its minimum
            │   │   │   └── it should revert with InsufficientAmountB
            │   │   └── when the optimal token B meets its minimum
            │   │       ├── it should push the funded token A and the optimal token B
            │   │       ├── it should mint to _recipient
            │   │       └── it should sweep the unspent token B to _caller at closure
            │   └── given the optimal token B exceeds the funded token B
            │       ├── when the optimal token A is below its minimum
            │       │   └── it should revert with InsufficientAmountA
            │       └── when the optimal token A meets its minimum
            │           ├── it should push the optimal token A and the funded token B
            │           ├── it should mint to _recipient
            │           └── it should sweep the unspent token A to _caller at closure
            └── when the full token B quote exceeds uint max
                ├── it should push the optimal token A and the funded token B
                ├── it should mint to _recipient
                └── it should sweep the unspent token A to _caller at closure
